-  "what_this_means": "With the FIXED generator the LLM tier answers essentially every call, yet the induced world model is REJECTED downstream on every cell and NO plan is ever installed. Both skip reasons are POST-generation gates, verified by code read: arc_competition_agent.py:5858 sets 'hidden_state_trust_below_threshold' after select_trusted_world_model returns trust_pass=False, and :5877 sets 'world_model_accuracy_below_threshold' after e3.WorldModelVerifier(active_transitions).score(engine) returns a gate value below the hard 0.5 floor. Both `return` before any plan is installed. So the generator's output never reaches action selection, and a first-win delta of zero is what the pipeline MUST produce at default settings -- it is a structural consequence, not a measurement failure.",
